## 🤖 Re-deriving with an agent

This change conflicts with what landed, and the merge engine could not combine them. An agent is now re-deriving it on your CI runner (re-implementing the change on the new head, tier 4b), from this pull request's diff, description, commits and linked issue.

The result lands only if it stays inside this change's files, passes the tests this pull request adds that fail without it, and is close to the reviewed diff.

<details>
<summary><b>Footprint</b> · writes 2 targets · affects 3 · 1 test group</summary>

**Writes** `shop::cart` `shop::pricing`

**Affects** `shop::cart` `shop::checkout` `shop::pricing`

**Tests** `shop`

Two changes conflict only when one writes what the other writes or affects.
</details>

